Veyra milestone suggestions
===========================

Current milestone
-----------------
- M0–M7 foundation, interaction, workspace, Components and vector-authoring UX are independently VERIFIED.
- Active work is `milestone.md` M8 — View Models, Data Binding & Runtime Data Graph.
- M8 must preserve `QUALITY.md`: projects without bindings should pay effectively zero binding runtime work, data evaluation stays DOM-free, and no second Component/state-machine/AI data model may appear.

Queued work after M8
--------------------
1. Resume master `plan.md` with full layered state-machine parity + visual graph editor.
2. Continue through Layout, listener/event/accessibility parity, drawing/paint/effects, text/media/assets, advanced rigging, animation-editor power, scripting/WGSL and production runtimes in plan order.
3. Translate the checked-in `deep-research-report (6).md` into bounded Lottie JSON + dotLottie milestones: masks/mattes, Motion Tokens/slots, packages/themes, compatibility analysis, import/export fidelity and modular runtimes. Do not silently collapse these into generic Rive features.
4. Introduce semantic shortcut/keymap profiles (Veyra / Rive / Lottie-AE / Custom) on top of M7's semantic editor-command layer.
5. Add bundle-size/performance regression tooling once a compiled/distributable runtime target exists; enforce `QUALITY.md` budgets instead of deleting parity features.
6. Build an interchange compatibility analyzer before broad export: exact / approximate / bake / rasterize / reject, with no silent feature loss.
7. Revisit the paused headless Node API/CLI only after the browser/editor contracts being reused are settled.

Editor follow-ups
-----------------
- Broaden M7 grouping beyond the current safe same-artboard + same-parent + contiguous-sibling contract only when Veyra has explicit semantics for preserving animation/property coordinate domains and stacking relative to unselected siblings. The current behavior intentionally fails closed rather than changing appearance silently.
- Add multi-selection transform operations (move/scale/rotate as a selection) as a later bounded editor-power milestone; M7 established selection/grouping identity but did not define shared transform semantics.

Longer-term lightweight/runtime principles
------------------------------------------
- Keep `.veyra` editable source distinct from a future compact `.vyr` runtime artifact.
- Use one evaluator semantics across editor preview and runtime.
- Prefer compiler stripping, dead-scene elimination, asset/geometry deduplication, font subsetting, dirty evaluation and settled-state sleeping over feature removal.
- Keep optional runtime modules such as text, audio, scripting, accessibility, advanced effects and debugging separable from the minimal vector/timeline core.
- Port to Rust/WASM/native only after evaluator/file contracts are sufficiently frozen and compatibility tests can prove semantic equivalence.

Guardrails
----------
- `milestone.md` remains the only active implementation milestone.
- `plan.md` remains the authoritative product roadmap; `QUALITY.md` is the permanent non-functional engineering contract.
- Future work stays here until the current milestone is independently accepted.
- Stable IDs and human display names remain separate contracts.
- UI convenience must not introduce a second mutation model or bypass the canonical control plane/Store validation boundary.
- No interchange exporter may silently drop unsupported Veyra features.
